# Enterprise Architecture Patterns

## Mục tiêu

Tài liệu này hợp nhất các nguyên tắc và best practices cho Enterprise Architecture trong Cursor Enterprise Framework, bao gồm Monolith Architecture, Microservices Architecture, Core Architecture, và Enterprise Architecture. Mục tiêu là cung cấp một framework toàn diện cho việc thiết kế và triển khai enterprise-scale systems.

---

## 1. Monolith Architecture

### 1.1 Mục tiêu

Monolith architecture là approach đặt tất cả components trong một đơn vị deployment duy nhất. Trong Cursor Enterprise Framework, monolith không phải là anti-pattern mà là valid choice cho nhiều scenarios. Nhiều successful systems bắt đầu như monolith và scale well với proper design. Modularity và boundaries quan trọng hơn deployment model.

### 1.2 Nguyên tắc

**1. Modular Monolith**

Tổ chức code thành modules. Clear boundaries. Loose coupling within monolith. Independent development. Can extract later if needed.

**2. Clear Module Boundaries**

Modules đại diện cho bounded contexts. Minimize cross-module dependencies. Module-first thinking. Team ownership per module.

**3. Internal APIs**

Module interfaces rõ ràng. No direct database access across modules. Service layer per module. Dependency injection.

**4. Transaction Boundaries**

Single transaction across modules. Can span multiple modules. Clear failure handling. Compensating transactions.

**5. Deployment Simplicity**

Single deployment unit. Simple CI/CD. No distributed complexity. Easy debugging. Full system testing.

**6. Performance Benefits**

No network overhead. Shared memory. Database joins across entities. Faster initial development.

**7. Operational Benefits**

Single dashboard. Single logging. Simple deployment. Rollback entire system. Easier incident management.

**8. When to Stay Monolith**

Small to medium teams. Fast iteration needed. Limited budget. Simple requirements. Startup mode.

**9. When to Consider Extraction**

Team growing beyond 10-15. Different scaling needs. Different technology requirements. Regulatory isolation.

**10. Evolutionary Architecture**

Start simple. Add modules. Define boundaries. Extract when needed. Don't over-engineer.

### 1.3 Checklist

- [ ] Module structure defined
- [ ] Clear boundaries established
- [ ] Internal APIs designed
- [ ] Dependency rules documented
- [ ] Testing strategy defined
- [ ] CI/CD configured
- [ ] Monitoring set up
- [ ] Module ownership assigned

### 1.4 Anti Patterns

**1. Big Ball of Mud**

No clear structure. Everything depends on everything. No boundaries. Hard to maintain. Add structure.

**2. God Classes**

Classes doing too much. Business logic scattered. Hard to test. Break into smaller pieces.

**3. Shared Database**

All modules share database. Coupling reintroduced. Schema changes affect multiple modules.

**4. Circular Dependencies**

Modules depend on each other. Hard to test. Hard to maintain. Break cycles.

**5. No Testing Strategy**

Monolith becomes untested. Fear of changes. Add automated tests.

